                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "563a5f4e-2fad-3cf5-afc2-6ee6e0dc8fcd",
                        "entry_id": "e803dff3-701c-3051-8308-eae2c24e2db6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "erster Faktor in einer Multiplikation; Zahl, die mit einer anderen multipliziert wird"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ecb4caed-f7ce-456b-98fe-36599bb44ce3",
                                "sense_id": "563a5f4e-2fad-3cf5-afc2-6ee6e0dc8fcd",
                                "text": "Der Multiplikator des Terms 3*6 ist 3."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "66550053-53ee-329b-9fe2-a665aef6e334",
                        "entry_id": "e803dff3-701c-3051-8308-eae2c24e2db6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Person oder Institution, welche Inhalte oder Wissen weiterverbreitet"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b06d8741-3c8f-45b7-825b-d02924739719",
                                "sense_id": "66550053-53ee-329b-9fe2-a665aef6e334",
                                "text": "„Wieland klopft an manche Tür, allerdings nicht bei solchen, die das nötige Kapital aufbringen könnten, sondern bei anderen Intellektuellen, möglichen Multiplikatoren seiner Idee, die er ausführlich schriftlich niederlegt.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7b30a6c4-b494-48c5-bbf1-6ea6fc774ced",
                        "source_entry_id": "e803dff3-701c-3051-8308-eae2c24e2db6",
                        "source_sense_id": "563a5f4e-2fad-3cf5-afc2-6ee6e0dc8fcd",
                        "source_sense_description": "Mathematik: erster Faktor in einer Multiplikation; Zahl, die mit einer anderen multipliziert wird",
                        "target_lang_word": "multiplier",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "multiplier",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "96fe5914-ab72-3bc0-ba0f-556b7b085398",
                                        "entry_id": "95fdf28b-8892-38cc-8f78-936fc38c533b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A number by which another (the multiplicand) is to be multiplied."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c1aec9d-fb70-4c9c-9341-d82fc09404e9",
                                                "sense_id": "96fe5914-ab72-3bc0-ba0f-556b7b085398",
                                                "text": "In the expression 5 × 7, the \"5\" is a multiplier."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a386106-e038-4a85-97c1-9bf94be7e35c",
                                                "sense_id": "96fe5914-ab72-3bc0-ba0f-556b7b085398",
                                                "text": "The score multiplier increases each time you complete a level of the video game."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78448a8e-5388-408c-811c-a584d9cc9187",
                                                "sense_id": "96fe5914-ab72-3bc0-ba0f-556b7b085398",
                                                "text": "The electron number constraint unlike the idempotency constraint can be represented by a single equation. For this reason, one can properly incorporate this constraint using a Lagrange multiplier and defining an effective chemical potential"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e166682c-6c30-49c6-bfe6-1e1a96b5f0d8",
                                                "sense_id": "96fe5914-ab72-3bc0-ba0f-556b7b085398",
                                                "text": "After studying a recursive formulation and the associated Bellman equation, in section 5.5 we analyze a Lagrangian formulation that provides useful insights about how Lagrange multipliers on transition laws relate to gradients of value functions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "050f4a91-ef09-4c39-b79d-c9dbc7791e00",
                                                "sense_id": "96fe5914-ab72-3bc0-ba0f-556b7b085398",
                                                "text": "But that can be ignored, because the USTR has set ε at 4 and φ at 0.25, so when computed give an overall multiplier of 1 for the imports number. And multiplying by 1 makes no difference at all."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5fcd1557-5e88-3183-b899-9eb638821282",
                                        "entry_id": "95fdf28b-8892-38cc-8f78-936fc38c533b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An adjective indicating the number of times something is to be multiplied."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d5e4fb6e-bfd3-4613-81ad-26c3502d7c3e",
                                                "sense_id": "5fcd1557-5e88-3183-b899-9eb638821282",
                                                "text": "English multipliers include \"double\" and \"triple\"."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cb168018-0ae7-30b0-91a8-38776faa5e45",
                                        "entry_id": "95fdf28b-8892-38cc-8f78-936fc38c533b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A ratio used to estimate total economic effect for a variety of economic activities."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b05ed9c6-6f7b-4cc4-9989-7692bfdb24cc",
                                                "sense_id": "cb168018-0ae7-30b0-91a8-38776faa5e45",
                                                "text": "There is a second-round effect of crowding in higher private investment as public sector contractors tool up to meet the public contracts, and then a third – as all firms adjust to the higher level of demand by raising business investment levels – of more crowding in and so-called “multiplier effects”."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1341f7e0-1787-3798-8d2f-f22479a47939",
                                        "entry_id": "95fdf28b-8892-38cc-8f78-936fc38c533b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of several devices used to enhance a signal"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1e46da3a-47fc-3c2a-a742-412882d650c9",
                                        "entry_id": "95fdf28b-8892-38cc-8f78-936fc38c533b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of several devices used to enhance a signal",
                                            "a coil; when Johann Schweigger in 1820 invented the electric coil, increasing the electro-magnetic field from a single wire, this invention was called a multiplier."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fff0f4b3-84a6-313a-9b52-ad8499e97207",
                                        "entry_id": "95fdf28b-8892-38cc-8f78-936fc38c533b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A multiplier onion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbba24b4-05d7-4a6d-bbcd-05d0e1162d3d",
                                                "sense_id": "fff0f4b3-84a6-313a-9b52-ad8499e97207",
                                                "text": "Shallots are the most prolific of all the multipliers, and easier to grow than onions."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fbd76bb5-5939-4916-8565-728eb115211c",
                        "source_entry_id": "e803dff3-701c-3051-8308-eae2c24e2db6",
                        "source_sense_id": "563a5f4e-2fad-3cf5-afc2-6ee6e0dc8fcd",
                        "source_sense_description": "Mathematik: erster Faktor in einer Multiplikation; Zahl, die mit einer anderen multipliziert wird",
                        "target_lang_word": "multiplicateur",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "multiplicateur",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cebc1a3f-c6bd-3c80-985c-8794ce65752d",
                                        "entry_id": "90aa8ce0-8591-3f12-82f1-fbdcda4004d8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui multiplie."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08f0ae99-4642-436e-b0a2-132b67e25a6c",
                                                "sense_id": "cebc1a3f-c6bd-3c80-985c-8794ce65752d",
                                                "text": "Un effet multiplicateur."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "multiplicateur",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f9ec1cb3-7345-3fcd-a332-b52f21c60f51",
                                        "entry_id": "d31a9d22-0df5-37b8-adb5-b12afae5374c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Nombre par lequel on multiplie un autre."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0970d09-f21d-4882-bbd0-8d87d9cf3554",
                                                "sense_id": "f9ec1cb3-7345-3fcd-a332-b52f21c60f51",
                                                "text": "Dans la multiplication de quatre par trois, trois est le multiplicateur."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98c98871-028c-4eb2-a895-c5a3c9282f25",
                                                "sense_id": "f9ec1cb3-7345-3fcd-a332-b52f21c60f51",
                                                "text": "Soit +A à multiplier par +B. La valeur absolue du produit sera composée avec la valeur absolue A du multiplicande, comme la valeur absolue B du multiplicateur est composée avec l’unité ; c’est-à-dire que, d’après les notations admises, cette valeur absolue du produit sera AB. Quant au signe du produit, comme le multiplicateur +B a le même signe que l’unité positive, ce produit aura le même signe que le multiplicande, c’est-à-dire +.\nAinsi, le produit de +A par +B est +AB.\nSoit +A à multiplier par −B. La valeur absolue du produit sera, comme ci-dessus, AB. Mais le multiplicateur −B ayant un signe contraire à celui de l’unité positive, le produit aura un signe contraire à celui du multiplicande, c’est-à-dire −.\nAinsi le produit de +A par −B est −AB."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
